# Git-sync working copies created by a locally run host (dashboard connect)
mockifyr-data/

# The demo is two halves and they need opposite rules (#321).
#
# AUTHORED — scripts, compose, the Keycloak realm, the deck, the runbook — is tracked: it is the
# thing that gets rehearsed before a customer call, and leaving it on one laptop meant it was backed
# up by nothing and reviewable by nobody.
#
# RUNTIME — what a locally run host writes, plus installed packages and logs — is not. Twenty-four
# files of exactly this once rode into an unrelated commit on a `git add -A`, which is why the rule
# is committed rather than living in one clone's .git/info/exclude.
demo/work/
demo/upstream/
demo/node_modules/
demo/*.log
demo/.*
src/Mockifyr.Server/demo/
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
